Phase 5 acceptance follow-up, 2026-10-04 UTC. No live Broker contacted.
P5-V03: scripted loopback rpc tests cover one Broker send attempt under sync/future timeout, oneway offset completion and expired deadline, unavailable NameServer failover, and no post-deadline NameServer failover. Per-method attempt coverage has not been established; gate remains open.
P5-V01: consumer/extension scripted branch matrices and producer send variants added; gate remains open until every public method and meaningful response branch is audited against a method inventory, including malformed success where a body/header is decoded.
P5-U01: Java 5.5.1 offline reply fixture differential verifies 15 response frames; new invoked MQClientAPIImpl mock-transport oracle checks send V2 oneway, query offset sync success, and route sync error. The remaining method invocation modes and success/error branches are not covered by executed Java invocation fixtures. Gate remains open.
Validation: cargo test --workspace --locked PASS; cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-core --locked PASS; cargo fmt --check PASS; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings PASS; mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify PASS; compat/java-reference/run-rpc-differential.sh PASS (15 frames). The Maven and differential commands emitted a fastjson2 sun.misc.Unsafe deprecation warning.
Phase 19 live P5-V02 remains pending; Phase 5 is NOT accepted while P5-V01, P5-V03 and P5-U01 are open.
Follow-up 2026-10-04: committed scripted domain matrix 19c8c44, all-public-Broker-method single-attempt loopback matrix d71609b, and expanded executed pinned Java oracle 7cc8671. The earlier 1200c75 oracle covered only three representative calls. Rust matrix now covers send V1/V2/batch/reply V1/V2 in sync/future/oneway, end transaction, consumer methods (including oneway update/unlock), heartbeat V1/V2, unregister, assignment/request mode/Lite/POP/ACK/change invisibility and generic request/oneway. Silent peer checks one observed frame, matching code/mode and no second frame/connection within a bounded observation window; timeout may surface as SendRequest when the peer closes. Existing route tests check unavailable NameServer failover and original-deadline stop; these checks do not prove arbitrary future retries cannot occur outside the observation window.
P5-V01 inventory: Rust tests in producer.rs check five send variants with four domain statuses, unknown code and malformed success in sync/future modes; oneway send and end transaction have no decoded success response to corrupt. consumer.rs checks pull's four status outcomes and malformed fields, offset not-found, consumer-list decoded body and lock response; update/send-back/unlock decode no success payload. extensions.rs checks heartbeat V1/V2, unregister, assignment/request-mode/Lite, POP/Lite POP, ACK/batch ACK and change invisibility, including decoded-payload malformed cases and ignored payloads on void calls. rpc.rs checks route success, not-found, unknown and malformed response. This is a method-level Rust scripted matrix, not a Java differential claim. P5-V01 remains unchecked pending independent evidence audit of every branch and explicit applicability decisions for each malformed-success case.
P5-V03: all exposed explicit-Broker methods now have a scripted one-attempt test, with oneway and send modes; representative NameServer failover and expired deadline remain covered. Keep gate unchecked pending review of oneway pending-state/deadline evidence across methods and deterministic timeout behavior; the attempt harness uses a finite observation window.
P5-U01 Java 5.5.1 method invocation evidence: actual injected mock RemotingClient checks send V2 ONEWAY/SYNC statuses and error, ASYNC dispatch only; pull SYNC four outcomes/error and ASYNC dispatch only; query offset SYNC success; update offset ONEWAY; heartbeat/unregister SYNC success/error; route SYNC topic-not-exist. The 15 response-frame fixture differential verifies frame decoding but does not invoke MQClientAPIImpl. Missing executed Java method/branch/mode evidence includes send V1/batch/reply variants, async callbacks/completion, route success/unknown/malformed, offset not-found/unknown/malformed and other consumer/extension methods; Java fixture/branch matrix is not complete. P5-U01 remains unchecked.
Follow-up validation: cargo test --workspace --locked PASS; cargo fmt --all -- --check PASS; cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings PASS; mvn -q -f compat/java-reference/pom.xml verify PASS (21 Java scenarios; fastjson2 sun.misc.Unsafe warning only); compat/java-reference/run-rpc-differential.sh PASS (15 frames). No Broker/Docker contacted. Final plan review: P5-V01/P5-V03/P5-U01 remain open; P5-V02 intentionally deferred to Phase 19. Phase 5 NOT accepted.